# =============================================================================
# North Forge - Hermes Edition (Kyocera Edition v21.8) - part of the North
# Forge project.
# File: .env.example | Script version: 1.1.0 | Updated: 2026-09-05
# Author: Kenneth C. Walker Jr. - Senior Technical Support Engineer, TSC
# =============================================================================
#
# Most people don't need this file at all. By default, North Forge launches
# with OpenCode Free - a free, keyless AI provider with no account and no
# payment method needed - and this .env is never created or touched.
#
# This file only matters if you deliberately type OWNKEY at the launcher's
# first-run provider prompt to use your own paid Anthropic API key instead
# (e.g. for heavier field/production use than the free tier is meant for).
# If that's you: copy this file to .env in the same folder and fill in your
# own value below. NEVER commit the real .env - it's already excluded in
# .gitignore.
#
# This is an Anthropic API key from console.anthropic.com (pay-per-token billing).
# It is NOT your claude.ai Pro/Max login - Anthropic does not permit routing
# Pro/Max subscription credentials through third-party tools like Hermes.
#
# IMPORTANT: once you have a real key, run 'hermes model' and pick a standard
# model such as Sonnet or Opus. Avoid a premium/credits-gated model (Fable,
# Mythos) as your default unless you specifically understand it requires a
# separate purchased "usage credits" balance on top of this API key - an
# ordinary pay-per-token key alone will not cover it, and you can otherwise
# get a "buy credits" error on your very first real question.
#
# Practical note for a shared thumb-drive deployment: anyone holding the drive
# holds this key if it's stored here in plaintext. Consider setting a spend
# cap on the key in the Anthropic console, and/or keeping the real .env off
# the drive and typing it in per-machine instead.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here
